    "text": "Usage: teamx actions resolve (--request JSON | --request-file PATH) [--tool ENTRY]\nVerify a target on the exact tools-list account; Lark tools run ENTRY actions resolve and GitLab root actions resolve --tool ENTRY select their managed entry.\nParameters: --request: {locator,turn_number}; locator is {self:true}, {query:{object_type:chat,text:NAME}}, a returned candidates[i].locator unchanged, or {target_ref:REF}. Root requests without --tool also accept provider; account_owner_seq is optional human account-ownership evidence. --request-file PATH: read the same JSON from a file; - reads stdin. Mutually exclusive with --request. Existing endpoint/body and business field limits still apply.\nCommon: --endpoint URL (bound TEAMX_ENDPOINT); --json (JSON output, default true). Requires the six bound TEAMX_* identity values.\nReturns: resolution: account, target/label or candidates[].{label,locator}, status, complete, candidates_incomplete and reason. target_ref plus actions: input_schema, required request fields, authority contract, executable and repair reason/next_action.\nExample: teamx actions resolve --tool ENTRY --request '{\"locator\":{\"self\":true},\"turn_number\":1}'; or teamx actions resolve --request-file payload.json (use - for stdin)\nConstraints: Candidates are unverified; resolve the selected locator on the same entry with the CURRENT turn. Clarify duplicate names; retain incompleteness. The service verifies identity, account, membership and permission. Reuse an existing valid target_ref. Saved message refs resolve ordinary replies; current production GitLab uses existing followup targets. Target access is not sending authority.\n",
